## ❓ Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)

#### Q1: Do quartz watches stop working if not worn?
No. Unlike automatic mechanical watches that stop after 38–48 hours of inactivity, a standard quartz watch will continue running as long as the battery has charge, whether worn or stored in a watch box.

#### Q2: Can a quartz watch work without any battery at all?
Only if it is a **Solar-Quartz** exposed directly to light, or a **Kinetic** watch while actively moving. However, without a storage cell/capacitor, the watch would immediately turn off once light or movement stops.

#### Q3: Is an automatic watch better than a quartz watch?
It depends on your preference! Automatic watches are prized for their traditional mechanical craftsmanship and sweeping second hand, whereas quartz watches offer far superior precision, grab-and-go convenience, and lower maintenance costs.

